==Battleground==
*1 [[The 6th Angel (Enemy)|The 6th Angel]] spawns as the boss after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*1 [[THE SLOTH]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*3 [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*6 [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*2 [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage can get pretty annoying at times due to THE SLOTH blocking your units from landing hits onto Ramiel. However, because there isn't much pushing power, you can chip down each Heavenly Hippoe with basic units like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dancing Flasher Cat]], [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]] and [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale Cat]]. Once the Hippoes die down, you can take your time chipping down THE SLOTH and then Ramiel soon after.

==='''4 Crown'''===
You can also rush The 6th Angel using [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]. Start the stage with a [[Battle Items#Rich Cat|Rich Cat]] and [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]] Battle Item, then turn off Sniper the Cat at 2,600¢. Summon Awakened Bahamut Cat at 4,500¢, and when Awakened Bahamut's first attack finishes, spawn in a [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]] to take an attack from THE SLOTH. Turn on Sniper the Cat once The 6th Angel is about to finish its attack at 6,500¢. If done correctly, the boss should die then and there, leaving the rest of the enemies to fend for themselves.

If your Awakened Bahamut Cat has the Explosion [[Talents|Talent]] maxed, you don't have to worry about timing. Bahamut will likely deal enough damage to stagger her long enough for him to land a second hit, wiping her off the stage in the blink of an eye.

